## H1: the cause is right, the fix is not
- **The cause is supported.** The matcher is `Agent|Task` (`.claude/settings.json:87`). A matcher made only of letters and `|` is matched as an exact list of tool names, and PreToolUse fires for every tool except EndConversation (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks). So a SendMessage call never reaches the hook, and rule (c) never fires live.
- **The fix is wrong.** Rule (c) refuses every SendMessage in a cycle session except one addressed to "main" (`guard_session.py:93-111`). "Count a SendMessage as a dispatch" would allow up to 8 of them, which weakens the rule. Widen the matcher only.
- **Also:** `guard_card`'s matcher (`settings.json:76`) doesn't include SendMessage either.
- **Test:** run a real `claude -p` session with `CYCLE_SESSION=1` that sends one SendMessage. G15-G18 call the hook directly, so they cannot test whether it is registered.

